hall be filled with mischief.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Lying lips are abomination to the LORD:¦layout ‚¤textÙ)But they that deal truly are his delight.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#A prudent man concealeth knowledge:¦layout ‚¤textÙ/But the heart of fools proclaimeth foolishness.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)The hand of the diligent shall bear rule:¦layout ‚¤textÙ(But the slothful shall be under tribute.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.Heaviness in the heart of man maketh it stoop:¦layout ‚¤text¿But a good word maketh it glad.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3The righteous is more excellent than his neighbour:¦layout ‚¤textÙ(But the way of the wicked seduceth them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ<The slothful man roasteth not that which he took in hunting:¦layout ‚¤textÙ0But the substance of a diligent man is precious.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ$In the way of righteousness is life;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And in the pathway thereof there is no death.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse